      "side": 1,
      "message": "`vm_map_pages_zero(vma, pages, num)` passes `offset \u003d 0` to `__vm_map_pages()` for drivers that encode a fake offset cookie in `vma-\u003evm_pgoff` during `mmap` and want `vma-\u003evm_start` to map byte 0 (slice 0) of `pages[0]`. However, `__vm_map_pages()` checks `count \u003d vma_kernel_pages(vma)` (which adds `vma_slice_off(vma)`) and calls `vma_insert_pages_slices()` (which offsets into `pages[0]` by `vma_slice_offset(vma, addr)`). If the driver\u0027s 4KB `mmap` cookie had non-zero low bits `(pgoff_4k \u0026 3) !\u003d 0`, `vma-\u003evm_slice_off` is non-zero, causing `count \u003e num` (`-ENXIO`) or starting the mapping mid-page.\n\n**Recommendation**: Please squash aosp/4368010 (`p3s_6.18_b16`: `ANDROID: P3S: mm: Map 4KB-aligned page arrays in vm_map_pages()`) into this change (along with aosp/4367599 from `p3s_6.18_b11` if squashing the `vm_insert_page_slice()` rework).",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5cdd064ac163813083596c0cdb5dbe9cd160f666",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
