      "writtenOn": "2026-10-30T01:31:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks, done.\n\n`vm_map_pages_zero()` now clears `vm_slice_off` too, so `vm_start` maps slice 0 of `pages[0]` and the PTEs still match `vma_slice_offset()`.\n\nI\u0027d rather not squash aosp/4368010, though. For `vm_map_pages()` it maps the same as this patch. For `vm_map_pages_zero()` it maps slices that don\u0027t match the address (through `vm_insert_page_slice()` from aosp/4367599), which `__access_remote_vm()` and GUP can\u0027t follow.",
      "parentUuid": "cbc238f8_2a8e3846",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "5cdd064ac163813083596c0cdb5dbe9cd160f666",
